{"kind":"github_issue","repository":"Trae-AI/TRAE","item":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/2466","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/2466/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/2466/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/2466/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/2466","id":4256507529,"node_id":"I_kwDONiYvnc79tSaJ","number":2466,"title":"[Bug] Custom model GLM-5.1 (Z AI Coding Plan) fails with error 4054 due to unrecognized SSE `progress_notice` event","user":{"login":"6tizer","id":260656772,"node_id":"U_kgDOD4lOhA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260656772?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/6tizer","html_url":"https://github.com/6tizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/6tizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/6tizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/6tizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/6tizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/6tizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/6tizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/6tizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/6tizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/6tizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":9,"created_at":"2026-04-13T16:49:40Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T09:22:23Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bug Description\n\nWhen using GLM-5.1 from Z AI Coding Plan as a custom model in Trae, the AI Agent frequently fails with **error code 4054** (\"Custom model internal error occurred\"). The root cause is that GLM-5.1 sends `progress_notice` SSE events during long-running tasks, which Trae's SSE parser does not recognize, causing the stream to be incorrectly terminated.\n\n## Environment\n\n- **Trae Version**: 1.0.18 (2026-03-26)\n- **OS**: macOS 26.4.1 (Apple Silicon)\n- **Model**: GLM-5.1 via Z AI Coding Plan\n- **API Endpoint**: `https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4`\n- **Mode**: Both Agent and Plan mode affected\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Configure Z AI Coding Plan GLM-5.1 as a custom model in Trae\n2. Send a request that requires significant processing time (e.g., searching logs or analyzing large codebases)\n3. GLM-5.1 starts processing and periodically sends `progress_notice` SSE events (every ~2 seconds)\n4. Trae's SSE parser logs: `WARN: Unknown event: Event { event: \"progress_notice\", ... }`\n5. The SSE stream is terminated prematurely\n6. Error 4054 is returned to the user\n\n## Actual Behavior\n\nFrom `ai-agent` stdout log:\nWARN ai_agent::infrastructure::adapter::llm::event: Unknown event: Event { event: \"progress_notice\", data: \"\"Processing_1776098203\"\", id: \"1293801935\", retry: None }\nWARN ai_agent::infrastructure::adapter::llm::event: Unknown event: Event { event: \"progress_notice\", data: \"\"Processing_1776098205\"\", id: \"1293801936\", retry: None }\n... (repeated every 2 seconds)\nERROR ai_agent::infrastructure::aha_net::stream: [AhaNetHTTPClient/Stream][Error] is_queue_continue false, error: ErrorEvent { message: \"Custom model internal error occurred. Please check the proxy response for details.\", code: 4054 }\n\n\nThe SSE stream reports \"ended normally after 3 messages in 9.9s\" — only 3 actual content messages were received before the stream was terminated due to unrecognized events.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nTrae should recognize and **ignore** `progress_notice` SSE events (and `context_usage` events), continuing to wait for actual `content` events from the model. These are heartbeat/progress indicators from GLM-5.1 and should not cause stream termination.\n\n## Error Frequency\n\nIn a single 37-minute session, this error occurred **8 times**, making GLM-5.1 nearly unusable:\n\n| Time | Error Code | Duration |\n|------|-----------|----------|\n| 00:08:32 | 4054 | 48.5s |\n| 00:13:29 | 4054 | 178.4s |\n| 00:14:29 | 4054 | 51.2s |\n| 00:27:37 | 4054 | - |\n| 00:31:33 | 4054 | - |\n| 00:31:43 | 4028 | HTTP 500 |\n| 00:36:08 | 4054 | - |\n| 00:36:33 | 4054 | - |\n\n## Technical Details\n\n- The SSE parsing logic resides in the Rust-compiled `libai_agent.dylib` (source: `apps/icube_server_rs/crates/custom-model-proxy-client/src/default_handler.rs` and `stream_manager.rs`)\n- GLM-5.1 sends two unrecognized SSE event types: `progress_notice` and `context_usage`\n- Z AI's official documentation confirms `progress_notice` is a standard event for their Coding Plan API\n- This issue also affects GLM-5-Turbo and GLM-4.7 when they send progress events during long-running tasks\n- MCP tool names are duplicated in the logs (Notion, Exa Search registered twice), contributing to larger request bodies (~78KB)\n\n## Suggested Fix\n\nIn the SSE event parser (`custom_model_proxy_client`), add `progress_notice` and `context_usage` to the list of recognized but ignorable SSE event types. The parser should log these at DEBUG level and continue waiting for content events without terminating the stream.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/2466/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/2466/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},"comments":[{"url":"http